eir rooms they shot  the actors individually on green screen  and then placed them into the scene  which aside from the actors themselves  was a full cg animation what's more it  was the first day of shooting for many  of the cast members  i feel like we really had an energy  together that that worked  number four  when we first meet luther we see him  casually going about his day on the moon  it's no surprise they didn't actually  film on the moon but it may surprise you  that almost everything you see is cgi  actor tom hopper was filmed on a green  screen while being suspended with wires  to simulate the weightlessness of space  very few elements were practical and  most of the time the only real aspect is  luthor and a part of his spacesuit even  his helmet was cgi  number five the epic war scene at the  beginning of season two was brought to  life with a mix of impressive practical  set pieces and visually stunning cgi a  lot of the rubble and debris on the  ground was real while the buildings and  all the action happening in the sky was  cgi and that tank rolling down the  street that was real the shell shot out  of it was cg animation as was when vanya  stopped at mid-air elliot page was  lifted into the air on wires and shot on  a green screen to create the effect of  her character stopping the missile put  it all together and the result is an  epic scene  what the hell was that the end of the  world november 25th 1963.  number six  when you have a character that has a  humanoid body with a fishbowl head that  contains a real-life goldfish you have  to get creative in bringing said  character to life when filming they had  an actor wearing the suit and bottom  collar piece of the bowl we see in the  show with his head later being replaced  with a cgi fishbowl they did have a  fishbowl head on set for reference but  it was only on a stick and didn't  contain any water or fish what a digital  the studio behind the fish effects  bought real goldfish and kept them as  pets what a digital did a phenomenal job  making it happen  surely we can come to some form of  agreement that benefits both parties  number seven  when we see the commission's inner  workings we are introduced to an  infinite room of workers be a part of  something  [Music]  so grand that shows the massive scale of  the organization in real life the room  is much less impressive they shot the  scene in a small room with only a few  desk workers in front of a green screen  they expanded the size of the room with  cgi and added hundreds of more desk  workers to achieve the scale they were  going for  who was the case manager handling me  [Music]  number eight  when klaus summons his ghost friends you  can rest easy knowing they're not real  ghosts and are instead the work of cgi  artists in the season 1 finale and at  the beginning of season 2 ghost ben is  completely cgi and when ben is trying to  get out of klaus actor robert sheehan  was acting alongside no one and had to  do his best to pretend to be pushing a  ghost back into his body  we hope you enjoyed that as much as we  did  number nine  all of the jfk scenes in season two were  almost completely cgi in some of the  wide city shots the buildings motorcade  and even the people are cgi when vanya  destroys the fbi building elliot page  was on wires on a green screen set and  even then they were mostly replaced with  cgi anyway and when klaus tackles the  man with the umbrella the motorcade  behind him and all the people in the  background are cgi why use extras when  you have an amazing vfx team  number 10  reginald hargreaves revealing himself as  an alien is a shocking twist we didn't  see coming for the reveal they built a  mask that resembled kung fiore's face  and had the actor unzip it and peel it  off his head underneath the mask on his  real head he wore a motion capture cap  the cgi alien head was added later on to  complete the reveal  number 11  the effects team spent a lot of time  developing all the warp and wave effects  caused by the powers from the characters  five jumping through time allison's  powers and vania's blast waves all use  the same type of viscous effect vfx  supervisor everett burrell described the  effect as going into and coming out of a  bowl of jelly because of this the team  appropriately named the effect jelly  vision we use my ability to time travel  but this time  i'll take you with me number 12  the scenes with klaus and his cult  involved a mixture of practical and  digital effects the bus scenes were  filmed on a big blue screen with fans  used to simulate wind the city of  varanasi was added using cgi  number 13  a lot of cgi was used during the white  violin final battle in season 1. banya's  transformation into the white violin was  accomplished using bright lights on set  which were enhanced with a cgi glow that  was added in later the theater was at  times a real set and other times they  used a cgi version of it like when the  explosion comes through which was also a  cgi simulation  number 14  the epic shop was created with both  practical and digital effects they  filmed it on a giant outdoor set that  had a lot of real debris surrounding  actor aiden gallagher there was a small  green screen behind gallagher and the  rest of the environment was filled in  digitally  number 15  the unleashing of vania's powers for the  first time was a big moment for the  character elliot page was filmed alone  on a green screen while the camera  rotated around them the rain and the  environment were added digitally the  result was the first display of vania's  true powers  those were some high-powered vfx for a  high-powered super team which scene left  you most impressed with its vfx let us  know in the comments and thanks for  stopping by at the things

